    {
      "id": "c03eb42f-e7a8-4a73-847c-639a46e30c39",
      "name": "Check run health",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        2900,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const data = $('Prepare rows').first().json;\nif (data.needsAttention) throw new Error('Available rows imported. Run '+data.run.id+' needs attention: platform '+data.run.status+', report '+(data.report?.outcome ?? 'missing')+', stop '+(data.report?.stopReason ?? 'none')+'. Inspect REPORT before scheduling another collection.');\nreturn [{json:{runId:data.run.id,outcome:data.report.outcome,importedUniqueRows:data.posts.length}}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "41338e3a-6690-4671-b640-3674d1b536b8",
      "name": "Read before running",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -660
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Telegram \u2192 Google Sheets\nManual trigger only. Connect your own credentials and test manually before scheduling.\n\n1. Create a Posts tab with headers: id, channel, publishedAt, text, url, views, runId.\n2. Select your Apify HTTP Header Auth credential on all FIVE HTTP nodes (Authorization: Bearer TOKEN).\n3. Select Google Sheets credentials and your spreadsheet in Upsert into Google Sheets. Keep match column id and Cell Format = Let n8n format (RAW).\n4. Review Configuration: example public news channel, 20 posts maximum, $0.05 event cap per new run. Change channel and monitorId for your own feed.\n\nAfter a Sheets failure, set resumeRunId to the original run ID. Import sequentially; do not run two writers on the same sheet. An uncertain start request may have started a run: check Apify Console before retrying.\n\nActor: https://apify.com/humming_cobalt/telegram-channel-watch\nPrice: $0.005/run + $0.001/post. Sheets/n8n may have separate costs.",
        "height": 580,
        "width": 620
      }
    }
